/F1 11 Tf
50 750 Td
16 TL
(4. RESULTS AND EMPIRICAL FINDINGS) Tj
T*
(DocScale achieves a state-of-the-art Macro F1-score of 94.6% on document layout analysis, outperforming previous baselines by 4.8%.) Tj
T*
(Inference throughput reached 142 pages per second on an A100 GPU, reflecting a 3.2x speedup over dense vision transformers.) Tj
T*
(Ablation studies confirm that multi-scale positional gates contribute 2.9% of the total F1 improvement.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. LIMITATIONS) Tj
T*
(Despite strong empirical performance, DocScale exhibits several stated limitations.) Tj
T*
(First, the model performance degrades on historical manuscripts printed prior to 1950 due to font irregularities.) Tj
T*
(Second, our current implementation assumes single-language English documents and does not natively parse right-to-left scripts.) Tj
T*
(Third, inference memory scales quadratically for documents exceeding 100 pages, necessitating future work in linear attention.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6. CONCLUSION) Tj
T*
(DocScale provides an efficient, verifiable framework for scientific document summarization and semantic extraction.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
